      "candidate_vs_random_conclusion": "Distributed Representation with Overlapping Subspaces. Layer 1 (PR=7.63/64) and Layer 2 (PR=5.96/64) exhibit low effective dimensionality, concentrated in leading principal components. However, causal sufficiency scales smoothly with dimension k without step-function localization (Layer 2: k=4 -> 11.3%, k=16 -> 40.0%, k=32 -> 63.8%, k=64 -> 100.0%). Top-k candidate units do not significantly outperform dimension- and norm-matched random controls (all Holm-adjusted p > 0.05). Modular subcircuits are definitively falsified; spatial task conditioning is mediated by a distributed, low-dimensional population code."
