      "mechanistic_conclusion": "Disentangled Ego-Motion and Memory Dynamics. Offline calibration proves the learned sensor displacement head has low explanatory power (R^2 = 0.120) and fails to beat the zero baseline. In contrast, the action-conditioned predictor delta_s(s_t, a_t) achieves strong calibration (R^2 = 0.504, MAE 0.0177m). Under hold/freeze dead-reckoning, action-conditioned prediction matches oracle odometry within equivalence margin (TOST p < 0.05) and significantly outperforms zero displacement and shuffled action controls (p < 0.0001). Under fixed blending, exponential decay attenuates memory by 0.35^K, pulling the goal toward the static visual output."
